Apple has begun inviting selected members of the media to a product launch experience in Los Angeles on Wednesday, October 28, according to <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://x.com/markgurman/status/2110584725983396061">Mark Gurman</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Black-Apple-Event-Logo.jpeg" alt="" width="2048" height="1152" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068830" /><br/>
In a post on X, Gurman described the gathering as an "all-day product launch experience" for touchscreen MacBooks, a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a>, and Macs equipped with M6 chips.<br/>
<br/>
Gurman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/08/apple-october-27-macbook-pro/">previously reported</a> that Apple would introduce the devices "on or around" Tuesday, October 27, with an online video presentation and a hands-on experience for the media. His latest post specifies October 28 for the media gathering, but does not say whether the product announcements will take place that day or beforehand.<br/>
<br/>
The touchscreen MacBooks are expected to be redesigned 14-inch and 16-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> models, featuring <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> displays, a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/24/touchscreen-macbook-pro-dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/04/oled-macbook-pro-significantly-lighter-rumor/">significantly lighter designs</a>. While earlier rumors suggested Apple could use the "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/12/macbook-ultra-six-rumored-features/">MacBook Ultra</a>" name, Gurman's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/08/apple-october-27-macbook-pro/">report from earlier this month</a> suggested the devices would remain in the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; family.<br/>
<br/>
